# LeakSanitizer suppressions (Linux only; FA_SANITIZE=address;undefined). Read through LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...
# Policy: only leaks of system libraries we cannot free (graphics drivers, X11, ALSA) are listed, each with its reason.
# A leak in engine or tool code is fixed, not listed. Format: leak:<library or function pattern>
#
# Mesa/llvmpipe (the software GL/EGL under Xvfb) keeps its screens, shader caches and LLVM state until process exit.
leak:libGLX_mesa
leak:libEGL_mesa
leak:libgallium
leak:libLLVM
leak:swrast_dri
leak:libGLdispatch
# libX11 / xcb connection and keyboard state kept for the life of the display.
leak:libX11
leak:libxcb
leak:libXi
leak:libXcursor
# ALSA's configuration tree is allocated once and freed by an atexit hook that does not run on _exit.
leak:libasound
